msgid "`byte_stream.h` defines immediate partial reads and copied writes with finite absolute deadlines. SUCCESS reports local byte acceptance, not peer delivery; BUSY with zero bytes requires explicit owner progress. No caller buffer remains borrowed after a stream operation returns. The optional `Nexus::LwIPTCP` client implements this face over the pinned NO_SYS IPv4 stack. Products still own the executor, peer selection, trusted time, entropy and shutdown/reconnect policy."
msgstr "`byte_stream.h` defines immediate partial reads and copied writes with finite absolute deadlines. SUCCESS reports local byte acceptance, not peer delivery; BUSY with zero bytes requires explicit owner progress. No caller buffer remains borrowed after a stream operation returns. The optional `Nexus::LwIPTCP` client implements this face over the pinned NO_SYS IPv4 stack. Products still own the executor, peer selection, trusted time, entropy and shutdown/reconnect policy."

