msgid "The composition initializes lwIP once and supplies a live network adapter, caller-owned storage and a positive receive-frame budget. All raw stack APIs, callbacks, network service and clients share one serialized NO_SYS executor. Call facade data/control outside raw callbacks; nested cross-facade mutation is rejected with BUSY. No socket layer, worker, scheduler, lock, name registry or maximum opaque pool is created. A successful TCP start admits CONNECTING; it does not establish the connection. Its first finite connect deadline cannot be extended. The existing byte face is a stateful handle, not a readiness proof."
msgstr "The composition initializes lwIP once and supplies a live network adapter, caller-owned storage and a positive receive-frame budget. All raw stack APIs, callbacks, network service and clients share one serialized NO_SYS executor. Call facade data/control outside raw callbacks; nested cross-facade mutation is rejected with BUSY. No socket layer, worker, scheduler, lock, name registry or maximum opaque pool is created. A successful TCP start admits CONNECTING; it does not establish the connection. Its first finite connect deadline cannot be extended. The existing byte face is a stateful handle, not a readiness proof."

msgid "TCP writes use official copied admission: a positive partial count releases the caller input immediately, while queued data remains bounded stack storage. Later output failure cannot undo that acceptance. Diagnostics continue to report that failure, and subsequent data/service calls fail until explicit abort. RX holds at most one accepted pbuf chain; refused chains stay lwIP-owned. Only consumed bytes receive credit. Buffered bytes precede orderly FIN, and peer half-close still permits writes. A frame budget bounds acquisition, not the total wall time of arbitrary raw callbacks. Each nonzero byte attempt may perform one explicitly budgeted network pass."
msgstr "TCP writes use official copied admission: a positive partial count releases the caller input immediately, while queued data remains bounded stack storage. Later output failure cannot undo that acceptance. Diagnostics continue to report that failure, and subsequent data/service calls fail until explicit abort. RX holds at most one accepted pbuf chain; refused chains stay lwIP-owned. Only consumed bytes receive credit. Buffered bytes precede orderly FIN, and peer half-close still permits writes. A frame budget bounds acquisition, not the total wall time of arbitrary raw callbacks. Each nonzero byte attempt may perform one explicitly budgeted network pass."

msgid "Official PCB allocation shares the bounded stack pool and its reclamation policy. It may progress pending closes or reclaim TIME_WAIT, LAST_ACK, CLOSING and lower-priority active connections, invoking other clients' error callbacks even if the new start later fails. Local rejection retains no new references for that client; it does not promise a globally unchanged stack."
msgstr "Official PCB allocation shares the bounded stack pool and its reclamation policy. It may progress pending closes or reclaim TIME_WAIT, LAST_ACK, CLOSING and lower-priority active connections, invoking other clients' error callbacks even if the new start later fails. Local rejection retains no new references for that client; it does not promise a globally unchanged stack."

msgid "After producers join, the owner consumes buffered RX and explicitly progresses and retries close on BUSY under the first finite close deadline. That deadline cannot be extended. Timeout requires explicit abort while storage stays live; abort discards local data and detaches callbacks. Successful close proves this client context's final stack access. The official stack may still own deferred FIN and TIME_WAIT state. Preserve the network adapter, global pools, timers and unchanged clock domain until the product's complete stack shutdown/restart procedure permits withdrawal. Client detachment does not prove global stack shutdown or MAC/PHY drain."
msgstr "After producers join, the owner consumes buffered RX and explicitly progresses and retries close on BUSY under the first finite close deadline. That deadline cannot be extended. Timeout requires explicit abort while storage stays live; abort discards local data and detaches callbacks. Successful close proves this client context's final stack access. The official stack may still own deferred FIN and TIME_WAIT state. Preserve the network adapter, global pools, timers and unchanged clock domain until the product's complete stack shutdown/restart procedure permits withdrawal. Client detachment does not prove global stack shutdown or MAC/PHY drain."

msgid "Ordinary TLS/MQTT consumers include `tls.h` or `client.h` and link `Nexus::TLS` or `Nexus::CoreMQTT`. Their public session types are opaque and expose no supplier headers or profile macros. Only the static composition translation unit selects `Nexus::TLSStorage` with `nexus/tls/storage.h`, or `Nexus::CoreMQTTStorage` with `nexus/mqtt/core_mqtt_storage.h`, to allocate the exact pinned backend layout. Keep explicit storage targets local to composition; fields are implementation state, not business control APIs or binary ABI promises. Products explicitly call `nexus_add_tls()` or `nexus_add_coremqtt()` to create the selected targets."
msgstr "Ordinary TLS/MQTT consumers include `tls.h` or `client.h` and link `Nexus::TLS` or `Nexus::CoreMQTT`. Their public session types are opaque and expose no supplier headers or profile macros. Only the static composition translation unit selects `Nexus::TLSStorage` with `nexus/tls/storage.h`, or `Nexus::CoreMQTTStorage` with `nexus/mqtt/core_mqtt_storage.h`, to allocate the exact pinned backend layout. Keep explicit storage targets local to composition; fields are implementation state, not business control APIs or binary ABI promises. Products explicitly call `nexus_add_tls()` or `nexus_add_coremqtt()` to create the selected targets."

msgid "The TLS profile is one serialized TLS 1.2 client/PSA domain using ECDHE-ECDSA P-256 and AES-128-GCM/SHA-256. It requires explicit DER trust, trusted UTC and a reviewed entropy-quality assertion. Its 64 KiB caller arena and 512 B TX stage exclude session metadata, transport memory and stack. Join facade users, abort the session, then stop the runtime; failed or BUSY cleanup retains its resources. The MQTT 3.1.1 profile provides clean sessions and QoS0/1; callbacks borrow incoming views only until return. Explicit DISCONNECT and TLS close report local progress and do not replace lower-layer drain or peer acknowledgement. The component contracts detail [network](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/network/README.md), [TLS](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/tls/README.md) and [MQTT](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/mqtt/README.md) ownership and fixed profile limits."
msgstr "The TLS profile is one serialized TLS 1.2 client/PSA domain using ECDHE-ECDSA P-256 and AES-128-GCM/SHA-256. It requires explicit DER trust, trusted UTC and a reviewed entropy-quality assertion. Its 64 KiB caller arena and 512 B TX stage exclude session metadata, transport memory and stack. Join facade users, abort the session, then stop the runtime; failed or BUSY cleanup retains its resources. The MQTT 3.1.1 profile provides clean sessions and QoS0/1; callbacks borrow incoming views only until return. Explicit DISCONNECT and TLS close report local progress and do not replace lower-layer drain or peer acknowledgement. The component contracts detail [network](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/network/README.md), [TLS](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/tls/README.md) and [MQTT](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/mqtt/README.md) ownership and fixed profile limits."

msgid "For both Ethernet adapter profiles, successful link output reports frame admission. A failed SETTLED TX outcome remains observable once through `nx_lwip_adapter_service`; until that observation, another link output cannot overwrite or reuse the TX buffer. Observing the error clears only the settled, unborrowed request. It adds no error queue or instance storage and does not reset the MAC, replay a packet or choose a product recovery policy. An ACTIVE or QUARANTINED borrow remains retained. The TCP byte facade keeps its existing connection-failure policy; frame-error observation does not promise recovery."
msgstr "For both Ethernet adapter profiles, successful link output reports frame admission. A failed SETTLED TX outcome remains observable once through `nx_lwip_adapter_service`; until that observation, another link output cannot overwrite or reuse the TX buffer. Observing the error clears only the settled, unborrowed request. It adds no error queue or instance storage and does not reset the MAC, replay a packet or choose a product recovery policy. An ACTIVE or QUARANTINED borrow remains retained. The TCP byte facade keeps its existing connection-failure policy; frame-error observation does not promise recovery."

