msgid "The owner initializes lwIP once and attaches with `nx_lwip_loaned_adapter_start`. Supply zero-initialized, disjoint adapter, TX, fragment-view, frame-slot and custom-pbuf-piece storage. Select a nonzero `slot_count` and at least `slot_count * base.rx_capacity` pieces, with fragment capacity sized for the actual provider geometry. MAC payload spans must also be disjoint from adapter, TX/view and slot/piece storage. Invalid acquired spans are released without delivery. All raw APIs, reference operations, callbacks, service and stop share the same serialized, nonreentrant task owner. Live or reentrant attachment cannot erase retained references or tokens."
msgstr "The owner initializes lwIP once and attaches with `nx_lwip_loaned_adapter_start`. Supply zero-initialized, disjoint adapter, TX, fragment-view, frame-slot and custom-pbuf-piece storage. Select a nonzero `slot_count` and at least `slot_count * base.rx_capacity` pieces, with fragment capacity sized for the actual provider geometry. MAC payload spans must also be disjoint from adapter, TX/view and slot/piece storage. Invalid acquired spans are released without delivery. All raw APIs, reference operations, callbacks, service and stop share the same serialized, nonreentrant task owner. Live or reentrant attachment cannot erase retained references or tokens."

msgid "Each frame slot copies at most 136 B into its own writable `PBUF_REF` prefix. That prefix covers the 14 B Ethernet header, maximum 60 B IPv4 header and maximum 60 B TCP header, including the fields that official TCP input updates in place. The prefix can include payload; a frame of at most 136 B is copied entirely. Only bytes beyond the prefix reference the original immutable MAC fragments through `PBUF_ROM` tails. Raw consumers must treat those tails as read-only and clone before writing. This is RX payload-tail zero-copy; whole-frame and TX zero-copy are not provided. ICMP echo uses the official copy-for-reply path. VLAN delivery, IPv6, DHCP, DNS and IP reassembly remain unselected."
msgstr "Each frame slot copies at most 136 B into its own writable `PBUF_REF` prefix. That prefix covers the 14 B Ethernet header, maximum 60 B IPv4 header and maximum 60 B TCP header, including the fields that official TCP input updates in place. The prefix can include payload; a frame of at most 136 B is copied entirely. Only bytes beyond the prefix reference the original immutable MAC fragments through `PBUF_ROM` tails. Raw consumers must treat those tails as read-only and clone before writing. This is RX payload-tail zero-copy; whole-frame and TX zero-copy are not provided. ICMP echo uses the official copy-for-reply path. VLAN delivery, IPv6, DHCP, DNS and IP reassembly remain unselected."

msgid "A retained head or tail pbuf reference keeps its frame slot and exact MAC loan live. The final custom-pbuf free only marks pieces returned; it never calls the provider or rearms DMA. Subsequent owner service or stop releases the exact loan after every piece's final reference is gone. A failed release retains the token and storage and closes further adapter admission. Products first close PCBs and join raw users, callbacks, queues and observers. Stop returns BUSY while any pbuf reference remains and detaches only after exact RX release and the existing MAC/TX withdrawal obligations. Failed drain never revokes a loan."
msgstr "A retained head or tail pbuf reference keeps its frame slot and exact MAC loan live. The final custom-pbuf free only marks pieces returned; it never calls the provider or rearms DMA. Subsequent owner service or stop releases the exact loan after every piece's final reference is gone. A failed release retains the token and storage and closes further adapter admission. Products first close PCBs and join raw users, callbacks, queues and observers. Stop returns BUSY while any pbuf reference remains and detaches only after exact RX release and the existing MAC/TX withdrawal obligations. Failed drain never revokes a loan."

msgid "Slot count is metadata capacity, not a provider capability or an ACK-progress promise. Concurrent acquisition also requires independent provider loans and enough descriptors for the actual frames. The maintained enhanced F407 and GD470 MAC engine supports independent held RX heads and reverse-order release in software models; this fact does not establish universal capacity, lossless operation or progress under arbitrary retained traffic. Products budget and release loans for their selected frame geometry and workload."
msgstr "Slot count is metadata capacity, not a provider capability or an ACK-progress promise. Concurrent acquisition also requires independent provider loans and enough descriptors for the actual frames. The maintained enhanced F407 and GD470 MAC engine supports independent held RX heads and reverse-order release in software models; this fact does not establish universal capacity, lossless operation or progress under arbitrary retained traffic. Products budget and release loans for their selected frame geometry and workload."

msgid "The selected loaned profile keeps two spare 512 B `PBUF_POOL` payload blocks; the copied profile keeps its existing 24 blocks. The 16 KiB arena and other fixed protocol pools remain unchanged. RX custom-pbuf metadata, 136 B prefixes, MAC buffers and the copied TX buffer are additional caller-supplied storage. TX and ICMP reply fallback may use the existing bounded RAM allocator. These counts require the curated organization fork's narrow exemption of the explicit custom-RX/custom-pbuf profile from the stock `PBUF_POOL`/`TCP_WND` sizing heuristic. Every other stack sanity check remains active. This exemption does not establish stock-upstream admission or complete SRAM fit. Nominal pool counts are not a complete SRAM measurement."
msgstr "The selected loaned profile keeps two spare 512 B `PBUF_POOL` payload blocks; the copied profile keeps its existing 24 blocks. The 16 KiB arena and other fixed protocol pools remain unchanged. RX custom-pbuf metadata, 136 B prefixes, MAC buffers and the copied TX buffer are additional caller-supplied storage. TX and ICMP reply fallback may use the existing bounded RAM allocator. These counts require the curated organization fork's narrow exemption of the explicit custom-RX/custom-pbuf profile from the stock `PBUF_POOL`/`TCP_WND` sizing heuristic. Every other stack sanity check remains active. This exemption does not establish stock-upstream admission or complete SRAM fit. Nominal pool counts are not a complete SRAM measurement."

msgid "C11 link-only external development probes use two frame slots, four pieces, a 2048 B main stack and zero libc heap. The selected images pass a 32 KiB SRAM budget. The copied-profile BIN bytes and caller storage match the same source baseline with the common TX-outcome improvement, for both reference chips."
msgstr "C11 link-only external development probes use two frame slots, four pieces, a 2048 B main stack and zero libc heap. The selected images pass a 32 KiB SRAM budget. The copied-profile BIN bytes and caller storage match the same source baseline with the common TX-outcome improvement, for both reference chips."

