msgid "FIG-32 is a reference host-test data flow, not a product architecture or MCU network qualification. Solid bidirectional edges carry the same ciphertext over two independent TCP connections: software Ethernet frames between the Nexus client and a test-only lwIP peer, then a host socket between the transparent relay and local Mosquitto. The dashed edge identifies the one TLS session, which terminates at the Nexus TLS client and Mosquitto; the relay does not decrypt or terminate TLS. Each lwIP process owns its own serialized stack and clock. {download}`Editable DOT <../../assets/diagrams/lwip-tcp-tls-mqtt-host.dot>` and the [network contract](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/network/README.md) and [maintained relay fixture](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tests/contracts/lwip_mqtt_interop/README.md) define this figure's source and lifetime boundaries."
msgstr "FIG-32 is a reference host-test data flow, not a product architecture or MCU network qualification. Solid bidirectional edges carry the same ciphertext over two independent TCP connections: software Ethernet frames between the Nexus client and a test-only lwIP peer, then a host socket between the transparent relay and local Mosquitto. The dashed edge identifies the one TLS session, which terminates at the Nexus TLS client and Mosquitto; the relay does not decrypt or terminate TLS. Each lwIP process owns its own serialized stack and clock. {download}`Editable DOT <../../assets/diagrams/lwip-tcp-tls-mqtt-host.dot>` and the [network contract](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/network/README.md) and [maintained relay fixture](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tests/contracts/lwip_mqtt_interop/README.md) define this figure's source and lifetime boundaries."

