msgid "Same task owner as every lwIP raw API/callback. Timer callback cost is governed by the fixed stack profile and application callbacks; this is not a hard bound on the entire invocation. The copying profile copies RX bytes before exact release. The explicit loaned-RX profile retains immutable payload tails until its custom-pbuf references end. A failed release retains its token and closes progress; stop retries release without feeding duplicate bytes into the stack. Inline and deferred TX failure remain observable before request reuse; while pending, new link output returns ERR_IF without admitting bytes. Success inline completion remains immediately reusable. Consuming an already-settled failure makes the TX request READY, without automatic reset, replay, adapter close or forced restart. The product chooses provider recovery; an actual unfinished borrow is never revoked."
msgstr "Same task owner as every lwIP raw API/callback. Timer callback cost is governed by the fixed stack profile and application callbacks; this is not a hard bound on the entire invocation. The copying profile copies RX bytes before exact release. The explicit loaned-RX profile retains immutable payload tails until its custom-pbuf references end. A failed release retains its token and closes progress; stop retries release without feeding duplicate bytes into the stack. Inline and deferred TX failure remain observable before request reuse; while pending, new link output returns ERR_IF without admitting bytes. Success inline completion remains immediately reusable. Consuming an already-settled failure makes the TX request READY, without automatic reset, replay, adapter close or forced restart. The product chooses provider recovery; an actual unfinished borrow is never revoked."

